          "source_excerpt": "and did not either the one or other, or both cast their favourable sextile or trine to the degree ascending"
        }
      ],
      "diagnosis": "The main statement can include the case in which both bodies supply a favourable contact. Its qualification correctly says neither does, so the record is internally inconsistent. The source requires absence of the favourable Ascendant contact from each body, in addition to the Moon-Mercury square/opposition.",
      "required_correction": "Replace the main negation with an unambiguous neither-Moon-nor-Mercury condition; preserve the ascending degree as target and the Moon-Mercury hard aspect.",
      "suggested_source_statement": "Moon and Mercury square/opposite, and neither Moon nor Mercury casting a favourable sextile or trine to the Ascendant degree, is interpreted as false news deliberately reported to frighten Lilly's side.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "requires_correction"
    },
