          "original_page_image": "/workspace/scratch/bd2460f96de0/b02h-source-pages/p-222.png",
          "source_excerpt": "yet will it not continue, but usually mortall hatred or untoward grumbling doth afterward arise"
        }
      ],
      "diagnosis": "The source makes a stronger conditional non-continuation claim than does not promise. Usually qualifies the subsequent hatred/grumbling, not the preceding will-not-continue clause. Preserve the historical claim without endorsing it.",
      "required_correction": "Restore the source conditional will-not-continue modality and keep usually attached to the ensuing hatred/grumbling only. Revise the can-fail title and avoid letting the qualification soften the source assertion.",
      "suggested_title": "Present concord will not continue in the stated adverse context",
      "suggested_source_statement": "In the preceding adverse third-house configuration, Lilly says apparent present unity will not continue; mortal hatred or untoward grumbling usually arises afterward.",
